{"agent":"recover-5g","data":{"by":"grok-4.7","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"A question with no preset options still has no answerable surface. `payload` builds `{\"questions\":[{\"question\":...,\"header\":\"Question\",\"multiSelect\":false}]}` and omits `options`. AskUserQuestion only accepts a multiple-choice input of 2–4 `{label, description}` options (the approval branch always emits that shape, and the agent must send this payload unaltered). Given a waiting question whose `options` is missing or `[]`, the tool rejects the input, so the person cannot type the free-text answer this branch claims to record, and `attest` never sees a transcript hit. The same builder also emits 1 or 5+ options unchanged, which the tool likewise rejects.","digest":"5df698aa7c1ef924","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:payload","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"HIGH","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:payload"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"Free-text re-check reads the wrong field. `attest` stores the typed reply via `E.answer(..., text=hit.answer)` and sets `outcome` to `E.ANSWERED_WORD`, but the new question branch of `verify` requires `h.answer == row.get(\"answer\")`. Given a free-text question whose transcript answer is `\"ship the patch\"` and whose row stores that string under `text` (or only as the answer argument) with `answer` unset, `verify` returns False and a recorded harness answer fails the level check. Multiple-choice is also unchecked: `attest` sets `outcome = hit.answer` with no membership test, so a transcript label that is not in `row[\"options\"]` is recorded and then accepted by `verify`.","digest":"267bfbe3a76debbd","family":"xai","location":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:verify","reviewer":"grok-4.7","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:verify"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":21857,"diff_sha":"a12a2dce7336804337031cc2b6da1e3c6e29fc09572f81923634c33771554745","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/fix-B-question-ask-unreachable","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":62.4,"family":"xai","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":8000,"model":"grok-4.7","output_digest":"aa78d5b5653b5897","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B-question-ask-unreachable.critic.grok-4.7.20261109T053158Z-e6365aee.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794202318.4398587,"family":"google","gate":"critic","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"}],"review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"620d7804ba95c09eb75fad96606f0e4689cd7cea","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/approvals.py":"100644 15d7703cc26afc64bda452add0b744e4d6f7bb9e","ddflow/api/approvals_answer.py":"100644 e675ae3f556df3f2a2be9dff2829a9a9cd147b49","ddflow/api/approvals_harness.py":"100644 c20d137ceb975113fb6cb7b110f77d883c9997ca","ddflow/api/reporting/overview.py":"100644 8a6bee1f74c1d83843d70f5c02a1625d81fe897a","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py":"100644 ce4cb98f789f031e9a4c91e725b63d7b20e977c4","ddflow/services/approvals/view.py":"100644 7c2d2c40af5eab5b83b7f037e48fd0717c7dbb79","tests/test_question_ask_surfaces.py":"100644 6c01da833563171a951cab3082c57485a35b3d2a"},"reviewer":"grok-4.7","reviewer_digest":"1857ec352c55ee94","reviewer_families":["xai"],"round":2,"rounds":2,"status":"REVIEWED","superseded":["1e1af2b4e9594757","7d34a10b8154d368"],"titles":["ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:payload","ddflow/services/approvals/harness.py:verify"],"tree_sha":"620d7804ba95+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"critic","reason":"2 finding(s)"},"id":"e16785e3e7713c3c3f3a5bf04","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":159679,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B-question-ask-unreachable","ts":"2026-11-09T05:33:01.154022Z"}
